Australian Product Guide — Priority commerce depth v42 current release record
Release date: 2026-08-17
Production source: GitHub main via Vercel
Canonical production domain: https://australianproductguide.au

Current platform: priority commerce depth v42 over the existing authority-depth, semantic Scout, illustrative consumer experience, institutional design, Decision Lab, My APG local-first workspace with optional account sync, universal search, comparison, buying guides, trust surfaces, responsive accessibility hardening and privacy-first analytics consent. Architecture remains lightweight SSR-first Node with progressive enhancement.

Catalogue truth: 482 maintained products; 90 populated categories; 178 represented brands. Current high-intent depth includes televisions 11, laptops 7, robot vacuums 9, washing machines 8, coffee machines 10, wireless headphones at least 10, smartphones 9 and earbuds 5 maintained products. v42 added seven manufacturer-verified Australian records: iPhone 17 Pro, Samsung Galaxy S26 Ultra, Google Pixel 10 Pro, Samsung Galaxy Z Flip7, Fisher & Paykel WH1260H5 Series 11 12kg washer, Miele WQ 1000 WPS Nova Edition and ASKO W4104C.W.AU 10kg washer. These additions were chosen to deepen meaningful decision coverage rather than pad catalogue counts.

Retailer-intelligence truth: product records can now carry structured exact-model non-affiliate Australian retailer offers with the verified variant, check date, observed AUD price and/or availability where current evidence is defensible. Product pages surface those offers separately from paid Amazon Associate pathways and state that an observed price or stock status is not a live feed or a whole-of-market lowest-price claim. Representative v42 production examples include Apple Australia for iPhone 17 Pro 256GB Cosmic Orange at A$1,999 observed 17 Aug 2026, and an exact Samsung Australia Galaxy Z Flip7 256GB Coralred destination where APG deliberately withholds a stale promotional price. Retailer availability, affiliate participation and commission contribute zero recommendation points.

Amazon truth: the previously maintained set of 23 independently verified exact Amazon Australia product destinations remains in place. Records without a verified exact Amazon destination continue to use transparent model-specific Amazon search fallbacks carrying the APG Associates tag rather than guessed ASINs. Amazon links remain clearly disclosed as paid links and APG does not claim whole-of-market price comparison.

Product-imagery truth: v42 introduces a governed data-only verified photography registry. A photograph is publishable only when its source type is approved, rights basis is documented, product match is exact or an immaterial same-model variant, and verification is dated. Amazon Program Content additionally requires a verified ASIN and matching Amazon affiliate destination. APG does not scrape Amazon product pages, reverse-engineer image URLs, fabricate real-product photography or treat third-party Program Content as APG-owned. No newly authorised product-photo mappings were populated in the v42 registry; where an authorised exact-model asset is not available, Production continues to use APG-authored category-correct decision visuals and explicitly does not claim product photography. Completing genuine photography therefore remains an active rights-and-source ingestion task, not a completed catalogue claim.

Evidence truth: new v42 records are desk-researched from current Australian manufacturer product/specification evidence. APG does not claim hands-on testing. Each record carries explicit best-fit signals, documented strengths, an important compromise, source-verification date, retailer-check date and next-review window.

Freshness and QA: v42 adds a weekly priority-commerce audit covering catalogue depth floors for major categories, exact-retailer offer integrity, image-registry validity and a regression control preventing deliberately blank prices from rendering as A$0. Existing image, Amazon Associates, source, governance, editorial, account, visual, platform-integrity and Decision Intelligence checks remain in the release pipeline. Pull request #45 passed the full configured release suite before merge.

Production verification: v42 implementation merged to main at bde5270a7b638e84da85e1c398e863883e7b6c12 and deployed READY through Vercel. Representative public verification on 17 Aug 2026 confirmed HTTP 200 for the homepage, smartphones category, washing-machines category, iPhone 17 Pro product page and Galaxy Z Flip7 product page; current catalogue/category counts and new exact-retailer rows rendered as intended; the no-price Z Flip7 path did not render A$0; and no Production runtime errors were found in the post-release verification window. This is representative release verification, not a claim of a fresh browser crawl of every canonical route.

Privacy/analytics: Google Analytics remains opt-in. Analytics storage defaults to denied and the GA script loads only after the visitor allows analytics. My APG remains local-first and usable without login; account status does not affect recommendations.

Release discipline: GitHub main is authoritative; Vercel Production must match current source; canonical public pages, changed data/runtime surfaces, retailer/evidence controls, image-rights controls, security/privacy behaviour and representative consumer journeys must be verified before closing a release. This record distinguishes current shipped capability from the still-incomplete genuine-photography rollout.